Krita Nova 77 - Filter dialog: a coarse preview while the settings change

While the settings of a filter or adjustment (Filter > ..., Adjust > ...)
are being changed - a slider dragged, a curve moved - the preview works at
a quarter of the resolution (level of detail 2: 1/16 of the pixels), so it
keeps up; once the settings rest for 0.45 s the preview is made again at
full resolution, and OK always filters at full resolution (a coarse preview
is filtered again). The first preview when the dialog opens is at full
resolution. Uses Krita's level-of-detail ("instant preview") machinery:
KisCanvas2::setNovaPreviewLod() raises the level of detail the canvas asks
for; with no level-of-detail support (no OpenGL canvas) nothing changes.
kritarc [filterdialog] novaCoarsePreview=false turns it off.
With patch 41 (only the visible area is previewed) this is the CPU side of
faster adjustment previews.

